        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="1076" n="982" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg982"/>

                <head>No. 612.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 10,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 157.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch from the United States consulate-general in Cuba, reporting on tonnage
                    dues paid by Spanish vessels there.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>




